    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p42-q57-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Write $\\mathcal{T}_2\\circ\\mathcal{T}_1$ as a single horizontal dilation followed by a single horizontal translation. State the new scale factor and translation distance in terms of $a,b,c,d$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Horizontal scale factor $ac$, followed by a translation of $bc+d$ units to the right.\n\nThe second dilation scales the first translation by $c$.",
          "worked": "Applying $\\mathcal{T}_1$ to $y=f(x)$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f\\left(\\frac{x-b}{a}\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\mathcal{T}_2$, replace $x$ by $\\frac{x}{c}$, then replace $x$ by $x-d$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f\\left(\\frac{x/c-b}{a}\\right),\\\\y&=f\\left(\\frac{(x-d)/c-b}{a}\\right),\\\\y&=f\\left(\\frac{x-(bc+d)}{ac}\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nThe horizontal scale factor is $ac$, followed by a translation of $bc+d$ units to the right.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q57-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Suppose that the result was the same either way, so:\n$$\\mathcal{T}_2\\circ\\mathcal{T}_1=\\mathcal{T}_1\\circ\\mathcal{T}_2.$$\nShow that $(c-1)b=(a-1)d$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$$(c-1)b=(a-1)d.$$\n\nBoth orders have scale factor $ac$; equate their translation distances $bc+d$ and $ad+b$, then rearrange.",
          "worked": "For $\\mathcal{T}_1\\circ\\mathcal{T}_2$, the first translation $d$ is scaled by $a$, then $b$ is added. Its scale factor is $ac$ and its translation distance is $ad+b$.\n\nPart (a) gives scale factor $ac$ and translation distance $bc+d$ for $\\mathcal{T}_2\\circ\\mathcal{T}_1$. Since the transformations are equal, their translation distances are equal:\n$$\\begin{align*}bc+d&=ad+b,\\\\bc-b&=ad-d,\\\\(c-1)b&=(a-1)d.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
